      "path": "research/restoration/runs/reference625-test64-v1/labels-016-031.json",
      "observation": "Strong recurring family resemblance in 023/024/028 (face shape, eyes, beard and smile), and 016/026/030 (eyes, mouth and broad facial shape). Clean-shaven 017/020/025 also share a recognizable facial template despite hair/angle differences. The cohort has some meaningful hair, skin tone and facial-hair variation, but does not look like 16 wholly independent identities. This observation did not change individual acceptance labels."
    },
    {
      "path": "research/restoration/runs/reference625-test64-v1/labels-048-063.json",
      "observation": "Several recurring curly-haired bearded face families, with distinct jaw, hair, beard, pose and expression variations. Diversity is narrower than FFHQ; hashes alone do not establish identity diversity."
    },
    {
      "path": "research/restoration/runs/reference625-test64-v1/family-resemblance-032-047.txt",
      "sha256": "709b8831ae06ac4b7f998ea99d99f482cbbb34141a276d12a54c2b70e7dbd740",
      "observation": "Strong family resemblance across this group: most share swept or curled voluminous hair, similarly shaped narrow noses, full lips, direct or slightly sideward gazes, black clerical shirts and the same soft architectural setting. Indices037 and038 look especially like neighboring variations; 035 and045, and 032 and044, also share facial templates despite age/hair changes. Graying facial hair and skin tone produce some variety, but the group still feels like a narrow portrait family rather than 15 strongly distinct people. This is a separate diversity observation and does not change individual labels."
    }
  ],
